## Original Content
President Donald Trump disclosed just over 1,000 financial transactions in the month of June in what appears to be broad reshuffling of his portfolio.

## Summary
President Donald Trump disclosed over 1,000 financial transactions in June, indicating a broad reshuffling of his investment portfolio. Notable moves included selling shares in companies like Meta and purchasing Berkshire Hathaway stock.

## Key Points
- Trump disclosed just over 1,000 financial transactions during the month of June
- The volume of trades suggests a broad reshuffling of his investment portfolio
- He sold positions in companies including Meta
- He purchased shares of Berkshire Hathaway


